SUMMARY:A Taste of Piedmont
LOCATION:Café Q
DESCRIPTION:Category: Food & Beverage\nPrice: Free / Included\nStatus: Avai
 lable\nTime: 5 PM – 9 PM\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/ev
 ents/209097\n\nLet your palate wander to Northern Italy with our “Taste 
 of Piedmont” dinner specials\, celebrating the rich\, earthy flavors of 
 this renowned culinary region.\n\nAvailable exclusively during dinner serv
 ice\, this limited-time menu showcases the elegance of Piedmont’s season
 al bounty—from silky polenta infused with truffle and black trumpet mush
 rooms to tender braised pork cheeks in Barolo wine\, and delicate porcini-
 studded ravioli. Each dish is designed to highlight the region’s signatu
 re balance of rustic depth and refined technique. Pair with a Barolo or a 
 crisp local white to fully savor the essence of Piedmont.\n\nMake a Reserv
 ation.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/209097
CATEGORIES:Food & Beverage
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-195306@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20261112T180000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261112
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261113
SUMMARY:5th Anniversary 'House Celebration: A Night of Gathering & Impact
LOCATION:Offsite: MGM Music Hall
DESCRIPTION:Category: ‘Quin Impact Fund\nPrice: Free / Included\nStatus: 
 Available\nTime: 6 PM – 10 PM\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.c
 om/events/195306\n\nThanks to the incredible enthusiasm from Members wishi
 ng to join the party on November 12th\, please enjoy extended seating opt
 ions at MGM as we turn the venue inside out for an extraordinary night of
  entertainment! Look forward to design inspiration\, nostalgic expressions
 \, and musical programming inspired by The 'Quin\, promising an evening th
 at we'll be talking about for decades... \n\nAs a reminder\, the clubhous
 e will be closed on this afternoon and throughout the evening beginning at
  3PM on November 12th as we prepare to welcome you to our temporary addres
 s at MGM Music Hall for the night. \n\nA schedule of world-class perform
 ances by EGOT-winning\, multi-platinum artist and producer John Legend and
  the Grammy-winning Gipsy Kings featuring Nicolas Reyes\, with net proceed
 s benefiting The ’Quin Impact Fund.\n\n6:00PM | Doors Open\n\n7:15PM |
  Welcome Remarks\n\n7:20PM | Opening Performance by Gipsy Kings featuring 
 Nicolas Reyes\n\n8:35PM | Remarks from The 'Quin Co-Founders\, Sandy & Pau
 l Edgerley\n\n8:45PM | Headline Performance by John Legend\n\nThe stage 
 is set. We're delighted to celebrate five remarkable years of The ’Quin 
 with you - the leaders\, creators\, innovators\, and rising stars of our c
 ommunity who are shaping Boston's legacy.\n\nEnter the password QUINMEMBER
  to unlock all extended and remaining theater and box seat tickets.\n\nPur
 chase Theater or Box Seats\nIf you prefer a 'Quin-inspired Residential Sea
 ting Arrangement on the Ground Floor\, a limited number of cabaret tables 
 (seat 4)\, and lounges (seat 8)\, are available on a first-to-reserve basi
 s. These packages begin at a $2\,000 commitment and include bespoke food a
 nd beverage packages.\n\nRequest Residential Seating Options\nShould you r
 equire assistance or have any related questions please email the dedicated
  Impact Concierge Team at Impact5More@thequin.com. We look forward to cele
 brating with you in November!        \n\n*Ticket prices vary by seati
 ng location and package. Tickets are reserved for members\, plus three gue
 sts aged 21+. Tickets are limited\, available on a first-to-reserve basis\
 , and nonrefundable and nontransferable. Please note that The ‘Quin Hou
 se will close at 3:00PM on this date to ensure access to this celebration 
 for the entire ‘Quin House Team.\n\n____________________________________
 _______________________\n\nKnow Before You Go \nWhat time do doors open\,
  and when does the program begin?\nDoors open at 6:00 PM on Thursday\, Nov
 ember 12th. The program begins at 7:15 PM.\n\nWhere can I find my tickets\
 , and do I need to download the Live Nation app?\nLook for a separate emai
 l from “Live Nation Concerts” with your tickets. Download the Live Nat
 ion app to access them for entry.\n\nHow do I transfer tickets to guests a
 rriving separately?\nPlease transfer their tickets in advance through the 
 Live Nation app:\n\nTap the Profile icon\, then “My Tickets.”\nSelect 
 The ’Quin 5th Anniversary ’House Celebration.\nSelect the guest seats 
 you wish to transfer and tap “Transfer to.”\nChoose a contact or enter
  their information manually.\nTap “Transfer Ticket(s).”\n\nHow can I c
 onfirm that my guests have accepted their tickets?\nThe app will display �
 ��Transfer Pending: Recipient Name” until the recipient accepts the tick
 ets. Confirm acceptance with your guests before they arrive.\n\nWhere can 
 I park\, and can I reserve parking in advance?\nMGM does not own or operat
 e parking garages. Rideshare is encouraged\, and several paid parking lots
  are available in the Fenway/Kenmore area. Parking can be reserved in adva
 nce through SpotHero.\n\nWhat is the bag policy?\nBags may not exceed 12�
 � × 6” × 12”. All bags will be searched before entry.\n\nIs coat che
 ck available\, and is there a charge?\nComplimentary coat check is availab
 le upon arrival.\n\nWhat should I wear?\nBusiness elegant or cocktail atti
 re is recommended—with The ’Quin’s usual invitation to come as you a
 re.\n\nIs the event 21+\, and what identification is required?\nYes. All g
 uests must be 21 or older and bring a valid government-issued ID.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/195306
CATEGORIES:‘Quin Impact Fund
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-209681@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20261113T140000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261113T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261113T153000
SUMMARY:'Quin Chat: The Art of the City - Why Cultural Philanthropy Matters
  Now
DESCRIPTION:Category: ‘Quin Chat\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 24 spots lef
 t\nStatus: Available\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/2
 09681\n\n2:00PM Reception\, 2:30PM Discussion \n\nTo celebrate Town & Co
 untry’s milestone 180th anniversary\, Editor in Chief Stellene Volandes
  and The ‘Quin Co-Founder Sandy Edgerley will host a timely conversation
  on the vital role cultural philanthropy plays in shaping Boston and its f
 uture.\n\nThe Art of the City - Why Cultural Philanthropy Matters Now brin
 gs together an extraordinary group of leaders from across Boston’s cultu
 ral\, civic\, and philanthropic communities to explore the power of the ar
 ts\, the importance of investing in our cultural institutions\, and the fu
 ture of philanthropy for the next generation.\n\nJoining the conversation 
 along with Stellene and Sandy will be Peggy Fogelman\, Norma Jean Calderwo
 od Director of the Isabella Stewart Gardner Museum and Joseph Henry\, Chie
 f\, Mayor’s Office of Arts and Culture\, City of Boston.\n\nThe discussi
 on will be moderated by Adam Rathe\, Senior Features Director at Town & C
 ountry. A Q&A will follow.\n\n*This event is complimentary and reserved fo
 r members only. Complimentary light bites and refreshments will be served
 . Cancellations made within 24 hours of the event\, or failure to attend\
 , will result in a $25 charge.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/209681
CATEGORIES:‘Quin Chat
END:VEVENT
