SUMMARY:The Scottie's Sessions: Live Jazz with Northstar
LOCATION:Scottie's
DESCRIPTION:Category: Food & Beverage\nPrice: Free / Included\nStatus: Avai
 lable\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/208597\n\nSlip i
 nto Scottie’s for an evening of live jazz with an unexpected edge as Nor
 th Star takes the stage. Featuring tap\, tenor saxophone\, piano\, and bas
 s\, the quartet brings a playful twist to classic jazz\, with tap joining 
 the ensemble as both movement and percussion.\n\nGrab a cocktail\, settle 
 in\, and let the evening unfold—one beat\, note\, and step at a time.\n\
 nReservations are not required.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/208597
CATEGORIES:Food & Beverage
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-209682@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20261113T190000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261113T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261113T203000
SUMMARY:'Quin Chat: The Second Half of Athleticism - The Athlete's Dilemma
LOCATION:The Muse
DESCRIPTION:Category: ‘Quin Chat\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 6 spots left
 \nStatus: Waitlist Only\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/event
 s/209682\n\n7:00PM Reception\, 7:30PM Discussion \nWhat happens when orga
 nized competition ends\, but the athlete in us remains? For those who once
  built their lives around practices\, teammates\, and seasons\, stepping a
 way can raise questions of identity\, purpose\, and how we care for oursel
 ves beyond the demands of competition.\n\nDr. Rich Joseph\, Harvard Medic
 al School faculty physician and Founder of VIM Medicine\, returns to The �
 ��Quin to launch a three-part series exploring what it means to remain an 
 athlete for life. He will moderate a conversation with Marcus Wilson\, co-
 founder of NOBULL\; Ben Bergeron\, founder of CompTrain and coach to multi
 ple CrossFit Games champions\; and Jeremy Bettle\, a performance and sport
 s science leader whose work spans professional sports and who now leads Vi
 tality Collective.\n\nTogether\, they will explore how we redefine ambitio
 n\, find new sources of motivation\, and build a lasting relationship with
  movement. It’s a candid look at life after the final whistle—and how 
 the discipline\, resilience\, and sense of possibility that shaped us as c
 ompetitors can continue to serve us for decades to come.\n\n*This event is
  complimentary and reserved for members only. Complimentary light bites an
 d refreshments will be served. Cancellations made within 24 hours of the e
 vent\, or failure to attend\, will result in a $25 charge.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/209682
CATEGORIES:‘Quin Chat
END:VEVENT
